+# Feature Specification: Cancel a booking
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-11 | **Status**: Implemented
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Customer cancels (P1)
+`cancel(bookingId, at)` cancels a booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Cancelling before the rental starts refunds the full booking total.
+2. Cancelling once the rental has started (at >= start) refunds 0.
+3. After cancelling, the equipment is free again for that period (`book`, `availability`).
+4. Cancelling the same booking a second time is rejected.
+5. Unknown booking ids, malformed `at`, and cancelling after the rental has ended are rejected.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `at` is an ISO-8601 UTC string (any instant, not necessarily on the hour).
+- **FR-002**: at < start: refund = total; start <= at < end: refund = 0; at >= end: error.
+- **FR-003**: A cancelled booking no longer blocks overlaps; it can be cancelled only once.
+- **FR-004**: A rejected cancel leaves the booking unchanged.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Constitution is an unfilled template; no extra rules apply.
+- The refund policy was not given; full-before-start / none-after-start is the simplest reading and is
+  isolated in one place so the business can change it.
